Open, permissive, resource-efficient architecture for massive multimodal capability testing, Model Genomes, adaptive RAG, and intelligent routing
Research snapshot: 9 September 2026. This document is designed to be handed directly to an implementation AI or engineering team. It separates verified facts about third-party projects from architectural recommendations.
1. Executive decision
The recommended design is not a single benchmark suite and not a conventional RAG stack. It is a layered system that discovers the empirical boundary of each model or tool, stores the evidence as a versioned Model Genome, measures how much external knowledge improves performance, and lets a cognitive router decide whether to use the model alone, the brain, tools, another model, or a composition of them.
The core principle is: never treat a model capability as a permanent fact. Treat it as a statistically estimated property of a specific model version, configuration, modality, task family, and test population. The system continuously re-evaluates uncertain and drifting areas.
