3. Evaluation core
3.1 NVIDIA NeMo Evaluator — campaign and integration layer
Repository — https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Evaluator [Apache-2.0]
Use this as the top-level evaluation campaign substrate rather than writing your own benchmark runner. Current documentation shows built-in benchmarks plus external integrations for lm-eval, skills, VLMEvalKit, gym, Harbor, and containers. It also provides a local interceptor proxy that can cache, log, modify payloads, and limit turns without an external dependency. [1]
Connection: Universal Test Planner emits a campaign spec -> NeMo Evaluator executes a batch -> result artifacts are normalized by our Result Adapter -> statistical engine updates Model Genome -> Knowledge Gap Detector decides whether more tests are needed.
