22. Final stack recommendation
Core permissive baseline: PostgreSQL + AGE, Qdrant, Tantivy, NATS, Temporal, DuckDB, Arrow, OpenDAL, NeMo Evaluator, lm-evaluation-harness, DeepEval, MTEB, VLMEvalKit, llama.cpp, Whisper/faster-whisper/WhisperX, ViSQOL, SpeechBrain, OpenCLIP, Diffusers, uv and Ruff. Add vLLM/SGLang only to high-throughput GPU pools. Keep LiteLLM as a gateway adapter with release-time license verification rather than making it part of the irreducible core.
The proprietary core should be the Universal Cognitive Fabric itself: Model Genome schema and update engine, Active Knowledge Discovery, Test Genome, Truth/Provenance layer, Augmentation Gain measurement, Capability Router, multimodal verifier orchestration, and license/policy enforcement. Those are the pieces that turn a collection of open-source components into the “brain” architecture described in this specification.

